      "name": "Original object-support controls - MIT",
      "description": "Original MIT synthetic images, generator, expected sample counts and projects by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors. No customer or third-party images. Native template matching finds three poses; a template region excludes the 35-pixel background hole. Clear and touching parts have all 616 samples; covering ten columns leaves 406/616 supported samples. Visibility filters before downstream/clearance pick selection. Touching parts still have full appearance support, but clearance rejects both neighbors. Required three intentionally fails the count gate and prevents a pick while preserving current diagnostics. This appearance proxy is not true occlusion, collision or robotic grasp certification. See README and truth.json.",
